Creating an isolated Python environment is recommended (Python 3.10 or newer).

With conda, using the file in this repository:
    conda env create -f environment.yml
    conda activate arcopy

Or create it by hand:
    conda create -n arcopy python=3.11
    conda activate arcopy
    pip install -r requirements.txt

Required packages (requirements.txt):
    openseespy numpy pandas matplotlib pillow openpyxl xlsxwriter python-docx optuna

optuna is only needed for the smart (Bayesian) shear-wall search. In a Spyder
console it can be installed with:  %pip install optuna   (then restart the kernel)

Run:
    python main.py
or open main.py in Spyder and press Run.

The interface is interactive. The program requests the required structural,
material, loading, analysis, and optimization parameters during execution.
The user may choose which analyses to perform and may skip optional dynamic or
reporting stages.

Each run is saved in a folder named after the run. After every step the state is
saved in <run>/_checkpoints, so a run can be continued, or restarted from any
earlier step, without typing the model again.

Example (4-storey, 5-bay frame, all answers given in a file):
    python main.py < examples/four_storey_frame/inputs.txt

Verification against hand calculations:
    python tests/run_verification.py
